 ## Overview
-Tileable Noise Generation produces procedural noise fields that are spatially periodic, ensuring seamless continuity when the output is repeated in any dimension. It solves the discontinuity artifacts inherent in standard noise functions at texture or volume boundaries. It differs from its siblings by enforcing strict modulo arithmetic on coordinate indices or by using Fourier-domain techniques to guarantee exact periodicity, whereas [Fractal Brownian Motion](22237-fractal-brownian-motion.md) defines the spectral summation strategy rather than the boundary conditions.
