 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [3D Noise Generation with Box Filtering](1323-3d-noise-generation-with-box-filtering.md)
-Generates a 3D tiling noise volume by initializing a grid with uniform random values and applying a 3×3×3 box blur to suppress grid artifacts inherent in trilinear interpolation. It differs from gradient-based noise by using value noise with explicit spatial averaging, and from simple value noise by enforcing seamless tiling via modulo wrapping. Choose this when a smooth, low-frequency volumetric base is needed without the computational cost of gradient calculations.
