 ### [Value-Noise FBM Texture Generation](16950-value-noise-fbm-texture-generation.md)
-Synthesizes procedural volumetric textures, primarily for cloud simulation, by summing multiple octaves of value noise with decreasing amplitude and increasing frequency. It differs from gradient-based noise by using pre-computed random scalar values at grid vertices rather than gradient vectors, resulting in smoother, less detailed textures that are computationally cheaper to interpolate. Choose this for efficient cloud density fields where high-frequency detail is less critical than performance.
